-- title:
--   Diamond automorphism as base change of the rational action
-- statement:
--   Fix $M\ge 1$ (as a nonzero natural number) and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and write $\Gamma_H(M)=$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) for the subgroup of $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ consisting of those $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ whose image under `gamma0Units M` (the unit of $\mathbb Z/M$ with value `Gamma0Map M γ` and inverse the reduction of the $(0,0)$ entry) lies in $H$. Let $F=$ `xHFunctionField M H` be the intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)` of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\mathbb Q((q))$, which contains every quotient `intSeriesC ℚ pf / intSeriesC ℚ pg` coming from weight-$k$ modular forms $f,g$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$ (meaning $p_f$, $p_g$ mapped into $\mathbb C$ give `qExpansion 1 f`, `qExpansion 1 g`) and `intSeriesC ℚ pg ≠ 0`. Let $\rho:\Gamma_0(M)\to\operatorname{RingAut}(F)$ be a monoid homomorphism subject to two hypotheses: $\rho(\gamma)=1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma_H(M)$; and, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$, every weight $k$, all weight-$k$ forms $f,g,f_1,g_1$ on $\Gamma_H(M)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g,p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ and every $c\in\mathbb C^\times$ with $f_1=c\,(f\mid_k\gamma)$ and $g_1=c\,(g\mid_k\gamma)$ as functions on $\mathbb H$ and with `intSeriesC ℚ pg ≠ 0`, `intSeriesC ℚ pg₁ ≠ 0`, the element $\rho(\gamma)$ carries `intSeriesC ℚ pf / intSeriesC ℚ pg` to `intSeriesC ℚ pf₁ / intSeriesC ℚ pg₁` in $\mathbb Q((q))$. Finally let $d\in(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ with $(\gamma)_{00}\equiv d \pmod M$. The conclusion is that for every $x\in F$ the automorphism `diamondAutHBar M H d` of $\bar F=$ `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of $F$ under `coeffEmb`, and `diamondAutHBar` being the chosen $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-algebra automorphism satisfying `IsDiamondAutHBar M H d` when one exists and the identity otherwise) sends `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) x` to `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (ρ γ x)`, as an identity of Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   This identifies the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$ on the function field of $X_H(M)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear extension of the rational $\Gamma_0(M)$-action $\rho$ at any $\gamma$ whose upper-left entry reduces to $d$ — in particular with the same index $d$, with no inversion. It is the bridge used by the subsequent results on the diamond automorphisms, such as their multiplicativity, their triviality at indices coming from $H$, and their behaviour on elements of the rational function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_diamondAutHBar_apply_coeffEmb_eq_coeffEmb_ringAut_apply.lean

